DSL 1
# M10 blueprint: an author-curated side table pairing a real exam grammar item (by id) with one
# course skill the learner can target practice on after missing that item. Kept as its own
# contract/file deliberately — never a field on GrammarItemRow (dsl/exam.data-contract) — so the
# certified exam content stays byte-identical and this table can be revised independently.
#
# itemId is a plain string, not `ref GrammarItemRow`: biome's ref/key checking only resolves
# within one contract's own --rows universe, and GrammarItemRow belongs to the certified `exam`
# contract (dsl/exam.data-contract), authored across many per-exam files. Every itemId here is
# instead checked against the real, live GRAMMAR_ITEM_ROW_ROWS by
# `polski.exam.grammar.GrammarExamSkillLinkTest` (a Kotlin-level AC1 check, not a biome one).
# skillId is likewise a plain string, checked against `polski.data.skills` the same way.

RECORD ExamSkillLinkRow KEY linkId COUNT 0..
  linkId: string
  itemId: string
  skillId: string
  note: string OPTIONAL
END
